Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\sin x\cos x=\frac{1}{2}\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\frac{\pi}{32}$ and then at $x=\frac{\pi}{16}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\frac{1}{2}$.
$$
\begin{aligned}
E&=\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{16}\right)\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{16}\right)\\&=\frac{1}{2}\,\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{8}\right)
\end{aligned}
